EXCLUDED — LICENSE INCOMPATIBLE
--------------------------------

  Depth-Anything-V2-Base    CC-BY-NC-4.0
  Depth-Anything-V2-Large   CC-BY-NC-4.0

    Non-commercial only, which would break the promise that users may use
    Voxframe commercially. Only the Apache-2.0 Small checkpoint is used, and
    the non-commercial variants are never downloaded automatically. A user who
    explicitly opts into one gets the restriction recorded in their credits
    output. See DECISIONS.md D-007.

  OpenAI CLIP weights       Custom terms

    Carry usage restrictions that would propagate to every downstream user.
    The LAION-trained checkpoints (MIT) are used instead, with comparable
    performance for semantic image search. See DECISIONS.md D-008.

  Remotion                  Custom (company-size restrictions)

    Free for individuals and small companies, but requires a paid license
    above a size threshold. Incompatible with the requirement that any user
    may redistribute and use commercially. Not used, including in the web app.
    See DECISIONS.md D-010.

  MoviePy                   MIT (excluded for technical reasons, not license)

    License is fine. Excluded because it holds video frames in memory, which
    conflicts with the requirement to process 60-minute audio without loading
    whole videos. See DECISIONS.md D-009.


NOTES
-----

1. WEAK COPYLEFT (LGPL)

   libsndfile (via soundfile) is LGPL-2.1. It is dynamically linked and
   unmodified, which LGPL permits without imposing terms on Voxframe. Users
   may replace it with their own build.

2. MODEL WEIGHTS ARE SEPARATELY LICENSED

   Model weights carry their own license, independent of the code that loads
   them. transformers being Apache-2.0 says nothing about the license of a
   checkpoint it loads. Each checkpoint is listed above with its own license,
   and this distinction is why the Depth-Anything exclusion above is necessary.

3. MODELS ARE DOWNLOADED, NOT BUNDLED

   No model weights ship with Voxframe. They are downloaded on first use and
   cached locally. Voxframe never downloads a checkpoint whose license fails
   the commercial-use test, even when a user names one explicitly, without
   recording that restriction in the render's credits file.

4. CODEC PATENTS ARE NOT A LICENSING QUESTION

   H.264 and H.265 are covered by patent pools (MPEG LA / Via LA, Access
   Advance) entirely independent of any software license here. No open-source
   license grants rights to them, because no author of that software holds
   them. Voxframe ships no codec and can output royalty-free VP9 or AV1 for
   users who prefer to avoid the question. See README "Licensing".


